            <ArticleTitle>Favorable effect of modest alcohol consumption to fatty liver disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5393-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3748/wjg.v19.i32.5393</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We previously reported that modest alcohol consumption was significantly inversely associated with fatty liver disease. Feng et al pointed out a discrepancy of statistical significance between our current larger scale cohort and a previous cohort. However, the prevalence of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease was higher in non or minimal drinkers than those in light drinkers in both cohorts. They also argue that some potential co-factors such as soft drink consumption and genetic variations should be discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
